  "caption": "Quinn, 42, sprinted for the bus and felt like someone had kicked the calf. Nobody had. Quinn's plan was to stretch it really hard.\n\nInner calf tears often happen on a sudden push-off, and after 40 our muscles' spring and power naturally decline. Aggressive stretching doesn't speed up healing.\n\nWhat can help: starting gentle, graded calf loading early, building single-leg calf raises until they match the other side, adding spring work like skipping and hopping when ready, and keeping heavy calf raises twice a week with push-off rehearsal in your warm-up.\n\nGet a same-day check if calf pain comes with swelling, warmth or breathlessness, especially after a long flight or time in a cast.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
